WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.114
Zones and conduits turn risk analysis into architectural boundaries.

00:00:04.114 --> 00:00:08.720
A zone groups logical or physical assets that share security requirements based on factors

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.600
such as function,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.320
criticality, consequence, ownership, and exposure.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.850
A zone should represent a meaningful trust decision,

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.560
not merely an existing subnet or room.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.985
A conduit is a controlled communication path between zones.

00:00:19.985 --> 00:00:23.577
It carries the data and services that the operation requires while enforcing the

00:00:23.577 --> 00:00:25.120
boundary's security expectations.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:29.670
Teams should document approved sources, destinations, protocols, direction, purpose,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.280
users, and administrative ownership.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:31.970
For example,

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:36.050
an enterprise reporting system may need production data from a site historian.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.610
That requirement does not justify direct enterprise access to controllers.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:44.140
An intermediary service in an industrial DMZ can replicate required data while reducing

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:46.880
reachability toward lower-level control functions.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.315
Zone design should distinguish systems with different risk and capability.

00:00:50.315 --> 00:00:55.080
Safety functions, control areas, engineering services, remote access, wireless devices,

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.670
and legacy equipment may warrant separate treatment.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:01.795
Conduits should also account for administration, updates, backups, authentication,

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:04.280
and vendor support, not only routine production traffic.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.910
Segmentation technology implements part of the design,

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:09.640
but a firewall alone does not create a defensible zone.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.200
The boundary needs current inventory, documented flows, secure configuration, monitoring,

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.920
ownership, and change control.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.650
Teams must also test that restrictions preserve timing, redundancy, failover,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.360
and recovery.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.510
Review zones and conduits when architecture or risk changes.

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:26.630
Cloud analytics, new vendors, temporary maintenance links,

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:30.400
and production expansions can introduce paths that bypass the intended model.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.250
The objective is necessary, limited,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.340
observable communication between assets with clearly understood trust relationships.
